    "title": "Enhanced Security Measures Planned for Rockefeller Center Tree Lighting on December 3 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago The Department of Homeland Security’s Countering Weapons of Mass Destruction Office will help secure the Rockefeller Center tree lighting in New York on December 3, 2025. The office’s Mobile Detection Deployment Program will provide staff and detection equipment to support a multi-agency security effort at the event.\nThe FBI requested that the Mobile Detection Deployment Program join the Joint Hazard Assessment Team. This team includes the NYPD, FDNY, and Army National Guard Civil Support Team. The team will assist with radiological, nuclear, and chemical detection. They will also use training previously given to team members.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
